Simple Definition of AWS Step Functions:
========================================
AWS Step Functions is a serverless orchestration service that helps you coordinate multiple 
AWS services into automated workflows so your application can run smoothly without manual effort.

📦 Example:
Imagine you have an online order system:
User places an order.
Step Function:
Calls Lambda to process the order.
Stores data in DynamoDB.
Sends confirmation using SNS.
Waits for payment confirmation.
If payment is successful, triggers shipping service.
Instead of manually coding all of this logic and tracking each step, Step Functions does it visually and automatically.

🔁 Why use Step Functions?

Coordinates multiple AWS services and microservices.
Manages state and errors between steps.
Supports human interaction steps.
Helps visualize workflows.
Cost-effective and scalable.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Types of Step Functions States 
State Type	Description
Choice	Adds if-else logic.
Parallel	Runs multiple tasks at the same time.
Map	Loops through a list (like a for-each loop).
Wait	Pauses for a specific amount of time.
Pass	Passes input to output without performing work.
Success	Marks the workflow as successful.
Fail	Ends the workflow with failure.
Task	Performs a unit of work (e.g., call Lambda, SNS, ECS, etc.).
